{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>My people are destroyed for lack of knowledge</b> — If this word is from the root דמות, it would be followed by אל with three vowel points, like אל מי דמית (Isaiah 14:16). And the absence of the word אל is because of cutting off, like ודמיתי אמך (Ezekiel 16:44), the meaning being that she will no longer give birth. After this: 'in your place will be a priest, and you will stumble soon; your sons too will die.' 'Are destroyed' — he says to the priest: by your lack of knowledge my people are cut off." "<b>Because you have rejected knowledge, I too will reject you from being a priest to Me, and you have forgotten the Torah of your Elohim</b> — The meaning is doubled: 'Because you have rejected knowledge' — for to the priest the Torah was given. Furthermore: because they are the judges, for 'the lips of a priest guard knowledge.'" "<b>I will forget your sons</b> — Far be it that HaShem forgets. Rather, the meaning is that the sons of the priest will stumble and go to destruction."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The phrase אחריה אל בשלש נקודות is ambiguous; rendered literally as 'followed by אל with three vowel points.' The apparent quotation 'in your place will be a priest...' may refer to 1 Samuel 2 or a paraphrased allusion, but its exact source is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:06.109632688Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}